            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Engagement</strong><br>\nThe Spanish Civil War profoundly affected Miró, prompting him to create politically engaged works. His \"Still Life with Old Shoe\" is a harrowing, personal response to the conflict, reflecting the turmoil and violence of the period.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Experimentation with Multiple Media</strong><br>\nMiró was known for his experimental approach, working across painting, sculpture, printmaking, and ceramics. His boundless creativity led to innovative works in each medium, often marked by a sense of playfulness and humor.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Recognition and Exhibitions</strong><br>\nMiró achieved significant international acclaim during his lifetime, with numerous retrospectives and exhibitions dedicated to his work. He received several prestigious awards, and his pieces were displayed in major museums worldwide.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
